      "text": "To determine the number of women who attended the party, we need to analyze the given information and use it to set up an equation.\n\n1. **Identify the total number of dances per man:**\n   Each man danced with exactly 3 women.\n\n2. **Identify the total number of dances per woman:**\n   Each woman danced with exactly 2 men.\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of dances:**\n   Since there are 12 men and each man danced with 3 women, the total number of dances is:\n   \\[\n   12 \\text{ men} \\times 3 \\text{ women per man} = 36 \\text{ dances}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the total number of dances per woman:**\n   Since each woman danced with 2 men, the total number of dances can also be calculated as:\n   \\[\n   2 \\text{ men per woman} \\times \\text{number of women} = 36 \\text{ dances}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Set up the equation:**\n   Let \\( w \\) be the number of women who attended the party. The total number of dances can be expressed as:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times w = 36\n   \\]\n\n6. **Solve for \\( w \\):**\n   \\[\n   w = \\frac{36}{2} = 18\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of women who attended the party is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
