      "text": "To solve this problem, we can use the concept of graph theory. We can represent the men and women as vertices of a graph, and the dances as edges between the vertices. Since each man danced with exactly three women, we can say that each vertex has a degree of 3. Similarly, since each woman danced with exactly two men, we can say that each vertex has a degree of 2.\n\nThe sum of the degrees of all the vertices in a graph is equal to twice the number of edges. In this case, we have 12 men and 12 women, so the sum of the degrees of all the vertices is 24. Since each edge represents a dance between two people, the number of edges is equal to the number of dances.\n\nTherefore, we can set up the equation:\n\n24 = 2 * (number of dances)\n\nDivide both sides by 2:\n\n12 = number of dances\n\nSince each dance involves one man and one woman, the number of dances is equal to the number of women. Therefore, the number of women who attended the party is 12.",
